ate d’effet le 1er Janvier 2011.\n     plusieurs séances et tournées de formation ont été                          Cette opération s’est traduite par la reprise de l’actif\n     organisées par la Direction de l’Animation                                  et du passif du bilan de cette structure. Toutes les\n     Commerciale au profit des Directeurs d’Agences et                           activités d’ÉQUIPBAIL sont reprises et seront désormais\n     des Chargés de clientèle.                                                   effectuées par notre Banque. Le personnel a également\n                                                                                 été réaffecté au sein de l’effectif de la BOA-BÉNIN.\n     Au cours de l’année 2010, la BOA-BÉNIN a initié\n     et exécuté plusieurs actions de communication.\n     Elles se rapportent essentiellement à la communication\n\n\n                                                                            14\n\n                                B A N K O F A F R I C A - B É N I N / R A P P O R T A N N U E L 2 010 A N N U A L R E P O R T\n\n\n                                                                                      1- The bank’s situation\n                                                                                      and financial results\n                                                                                                 for fiscal year 2010\n\n                Journée mondiale du refugié\n                                                                             In 2010, BANK OF AFRICA – BENIN (BOA-BENIN) continued to expand its network with\n                    World Refugee Day.\n                                                                             the opening of nine new branches: seven in Cotonou (Cocotomey, Gbedjromèdé,\n                                                                             Dantopka, Aïdjedo, Zogbo, PK 10 and PK 7) and two regional (Allada and Natitingou).\n                                                                             Construction has been completed on two other branches (Parakou 3 and Kandi),\n                                                                             which are expected to open in the first quarter of 2011, thus raising the number of\n                                                                             branches to 37.\n                                                                             To staff these new branches and to replace departing personnel (resignations and\n                                                                             dismissals), we recruited 77 new employees in 2010, raising the total to 439.\n                                                                             Apart from banking diplomas, training was undertaken in several other areas, including\n                                                                             IT security, commercial and managerial techniques, management of banking risk,\n                                                                             risk mapping, taxes, OHADA legislation, management of payment incidents, IFRS,\n                                                                             anti-money laundering and others.\n                                                                             Commercially, we brought out new services and products, including PACK SALARIA and\n                                                                             T-CASH. And for better control over our marketing policy, several training sessions\n                                                                             and tours were organised by the Direction de l’Animation Commerciale for branch\n                                                                             managers and customer account managers.\n                                                                             During 2010, BOA-BENIN initiated and implemented several communication campaigns:\n                                                                             mainly to promote products and services to customers, to publicise its new branches,\n                                                                             and a corporate communication campaign. In addition, citizen initiatives were taken in the\n                                                                             areas of the environment, social issues and healthcare, among others. These include\n        Les guichets de l’Agence Aïdjédo, à Cotonou.                         BOA-BENIN’s participation, alongside the Ministry of the Environment and Protection\n         Counters at the Aïdjédo Branch, in Cotonou.                         of Nature (MEPN) and the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP), in organising\n                                                                             the 39th World Environment Day, and BOA-BENIN’s assistance to post-earthquake Haiti and\n                                                                             to Beninese victims of the June 2010 flooding.\n     Les comptes de bilan et de résultat\n                                                                             There were also several promotional campaigns to mark the Bank’s 20th anniversary and\n                                                                             the 50th anniversary of Benin’s independence.\nD’une année à l’autre, le total bilan a régressé\n                                                                             All these initiatives helped make the bank, its products, services and activities better\nd’environ 7,8 % passant de 491,1 milliards de\n                                                                             known, and to reinforce its civic commitment – in a word, to better establish the\nF CFA à 487,3 milliards de F CFA. Cette régression\n      