 still felt the effects, owing mainly to generally weaker demand for\n                                                            raw materials and lower migrant remittances.\n\n                                                            The Beninese economy\n     l’environnement juridique des affaires et la dispo-    Domestic economic activity was subject to the aftershocks of the international and regional\n                                                            economic environment described above.\n  nibilité d’une administration publique véritablement\n                                                            Due to both the impact of the international crisis and domestic causes, the domestic economic\n  au service du développement ;                             environment worsened significantly in 2009. This deterioration came in several forms, some\n      l’éradication de l’insécurité foncière, les projets   of which were only indirectly linked to the international crisis:\n                                                                 first of all, Nigeria was hit hard by the drop in oil prices, experienced sharp\n  tels que ceux du Millenium Challenge Account (MCA)        readjustments in most stock prices, and allowed its currency to float during most of the year;\n  ayant eu en ce domaine un impact encore très limité ;          the direct consequence for Benin of this situation was a notable decline in cross-border\n     la restauration des infrastructures - télécommuni-     trade, as CFAF-denominated products became much more expensive for Nigerian buyers:\n                                                            activity in the port of Cotonou experienced a marked decline, and customs receipts\n  cations, électricité - qui constituent une condition      encountered a major shortfall, which was not offset by stagnant tax receipts;\n  essentielle de tout décollage économique ;                     more generally, GDP growth in 2009 was far below